Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||06-21-2001||11:36 PM||||I might be able to get my hands on a 396 from a late 60s model chevelle SS. While the prospect of going from the 100 HP iron duke to 350+ HP goodness seems exciting, I really dont know if the engines will swap...anybody know? What other considerations should I take if I do this swap? do I need a kit? will it bolt up to the dukes 5 speed manual tranny? or should i find another tranny? are there any other things I should know about? I have an 88 coupe in very good shape, but its just too underpowered to get me from point a to point b (I do alot of mountain travel) and I would really like to waste my friend in his riced out MR2...||||reg||1
Z||000001||BV MotorSports||06-21-2001||11:48 PM||||While I have never seen a mid mounted big block v8 fiero...I hear there is atleast one out there. Having done a few SBC v8 swaps, I cant imagine the grief of stuffing a BBC mid mounted! Oh the horror!<BR>I have seen a front mounted BBC v8 fiero.<BR>A 3.8 v6 fiero would be pretty fast. Much easier for a 1st time swapper.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||4
